  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Scaling up Malaria prevention and control for universal coverage to achieve pre-elimination stage in the Gambia - Gambia (01-Jan-2013-30-Jun-2016)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In Gambia, malaria is holo- to meso-endemic with highly seasonal variation. The program supported by this grant aims to scale up the country&amp;#39;s efforts to eliminate malaria among its population. The program will focus on the diagnosis of malaria, using microscopy and rapid diagnostic tests; treatment at health facilities; and the scaling up of home management of malaria and of indoor residual spraying. The program also aims to scale up the distribution of long-lasting insecticidal nets and behavior change communication activities.</narrative>
  </description>
